I've been playing Nethack on and off for about a decade, with no
ascensions to my name.  I almost always played a Wizard.  Recently,
after another revival of interest inspired by browsing around on the
Nethack Wiki, I started again, this time playing a Valkyrie, reputedly
one of the easier classes to ascend.  After a few quickie deaths, I
got a nice strong game going.  Many hours this past weekend went into
it.  I was wreaking havoc with +2 Excalibur.  I got silver dragon
scale mail from a magic lamp wish in Minetown.  With my AC down to
-25, I was feeling pretty invincible; my max HP were up around 110,
but I rarely fell below 100.  The only problem was that I was
accumulating a ton of useful items that I never needed.  I left some
excess in a couple of stashes, but it was still hard to avoid becoming
burdened, even with the bag of holding from Sokoban.  Even so, I
always carefully lightened my load whenever it got too heavy.  Always,
until the one time...

...when I headed downstairs while wielding a cockatrice corpse.

AUGH.

And it's this month's featured freaking article on nethack.wikia.com,
too.

Although I'd sworn off savescumming, I immediately went desperately
hunting for a save file, but it was already gone.

Sigh.  Back to the grind, after a few days' break to get over the
disappointment.


